job_description:
Position Overview

The Data Analyst will help our team build massively scalable consumer systems for clean energy. The Analyst will help with data direction for all engineering solutions at Hanwha Q Cells and will also lead the way in building systems to data platform and data focused organization. The duties and responsibilities of a data analyst include more than collecting and analyzing data... They also must make this data accessible to those who need the information to streamline business processe s.

Responsibilities
• Uses programs to extract information from data sets and identify correlations and patterns;
• Organizes and transforms information into comprehensible structures;
• Uses analytical data to predict trends in the customer data as a whole and performs statistical analysis of data;
• Uses tools and techniques to visualize data in easy-to-understand formats, such as diagrams and graphs;
• Prepares reports and effectively presents to management and clients;
• Identifies and recommends new ways to save money by streamlining business processes;
• Monitors data quality and removes corrupt data;
• Communicates with stakeholders to understand data content and business requirements;
• Documents data requirements and enables data access to business owners through products such as ERP, CRM, and other applications.

REQUIREMENT
• At least two years of experience as a data analyst using analytics software and platforms;
• Sound knowledge of cloud infrastructure such as AWS and/or GCP;
• Excellent verbal and written communication skills to effectively present reports and documents to leadership and to junior members of the team;
• Critical and strategic thinking skills;
• Ability to prioritize multiple and simultaneous projects, issues, and activities;
• 2 years of Tableau Experience;
• Strong SQL Skills;
• Experience in building Tableau Dashboards;
• Hands-on experience with SQL database design;

Preferred Qualifications
• Familiarity with Cloud Data Services;
• Experience with Data Modeling software;
• Experience with CRM and other such software applications;
• Understanding of Data usage and data requirements;
• BS degree in Engineering or Math.

Physical, Mental, & Physical Demands

To comply with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 the essential physical, mental and environmental requirements for this job are listed below. These are requirements normally expected to perform regular job duties. Incumbent must be able to successfully perform all of the functions of the job with or without reasonable accommodation.

Mobility

Standing: 20% of time

Sitting: 70% of time

Walking: 10% of time

Strength

Pulling: up to 10 Pounds

Pushing: up to 10 Pounds

Carrying: up to 10 Pounds

Lifting: up to 10 Pounds

Agility(F = Frequently, O = Occasionally, N = Never)

Turning: F

Twisting: F

Bending: O

Crouching: O

Balancing: N

Climbing: N

Crawling: N

Kneeling: N

Dexterity(F = Frequently, O = Occasionally, N = Never)

Typing: F

Handling: F

Reaching: F

Accurately and promptly collect information on competitors, customers, and the industrial chain market, organize and report it; establish a rich source of data information channels;
Combine the information from research and communication to analyze the market layout and the situation in key areas, judge the changes in market trends, write market analysis reports, and provide support for sales work and future market planning;
According to the leadership's requirements, combine market development and business needs to periodically carry out special market insights, customer needs, and other specific research plans, implement the research, produce research reports, and propose corresponding strategic suggestions;
Organize and collect monthly market reports and monthly sales analysis reports on time;
Timely complete other tasks arranged by the leadership.
Job Requirements:
Minimum 2-3 years working experience in sales or production analysis for Manufacturing company.
Proficient with SQL software.
Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively within an executive team.
Meticulous attention to detail and excellent organizational skills.
Exceptionally proficient in both written and spoken English and Mandarin.
Proficiency in Microsoft Excel, Word, Power point, etc.

Job Description
Assist in conducting Quarterly Compliance Testing;
Assist in preparation of daily analysis to meet authority requirement;
Assist in compilation of information required by the law enforcement agencies;
Assist in preparation of meeting materials for the Senior Management;
Assist in compilation periodic statistic to be submitted to Authority.
Job Requirements
Posses a Bachelor’s Degree Actuarial Science, Statistic or Business Admin;
Good interpersonal & communication skills;
Ability to work independently as well as a team player;
Possess good time management, organizing and planning skills;
Must be analytical, resourceful and result-orientated;
SAS and Qlikview knowledge will be an advantage.
Fresh graduates are encouraged to apply.
